_🇸🇪 Denna artikel finns även på [svenska](/sm-mtbo-uppsala-2026-pm) 🇸🇪_

Welcome to Uppsala and the **Swedish Mountain Bike Orienteering Championships 2026**! Here you will find the official competition bulletin (PM) for all three races over the weekend, as well as food pre-order details and evening dinner information.

---

## Programme Overview

- **Saturday 15 August (Morning):** Middle Distance (Arena: OK Linné Clubhouse)
- **Saturday 15 August (Afternoon):** Sprint Distance (Arena: Syltahallen, Ultuna)
- **Saturday 15 August (Evening):** Championship Dinner & Prize Giving (Ulls Restaurant, SLU/Ultuna)
- **Sunday 16 August (Morning):** Long Distance (Arena: OK Linné Clubhouse)

---

## Middle Distance – Saturday 15 August

- **Arena:** OK Linné Clubhouse, Tallbacksvägen 68 in SW Uppsala (GPS: `59.828125, 17.610964`). Signposted from Norbyvägen.
- **Parking:** Adjacent to the arena, max 300 m.
- **Map:** Scale 1:7,500, contour interval 2.5 m. Created 2019, revised 2026.
- **Terrain:** The opening section features flat, park-like forest with a dense trail network and excellent rideability. Watch out for oncoming competitors and general public! After passing through a residential area – where mandatory passage through a road tunnel **must** be used – the course finishes in undulating forest terrain with technically demanding riding in places.
- **Traffic Rules:** Swedish traffic regulations and road signs must be strictly obeyed. Show courtesy in traffic and follow officials' instructions.
- **Start:** First start at **10:00**. Tarmac road to start, 800 m. Maps to start are collected at bib pickup at the arena.
- **Open Classes:** Short, Medium, and Long. Direct registration at the arena between 09:30–11:00.
- **Maximum Time:** 2.5 hours.
- **Prize Giving:** Prize giving for Saturday's Middle and Sprint distances will take place during the dinner at Ulls Restaurant on Ultuna on Saturday evening.
- **Officials:** Course Setter Berth-Arne Bengtsson (L-100 IF), Course Controller Mats Tibell.

---

## Sprint Distance – Saturday 15 August

- **Arena:** Syltahallen at Ultuna, Duhrevägen 4, approx. 7 km S of Uppsala C (GPS: `59.813883, 17.664988`). Signposted from Dag Hammarskjölds väg.
- **Parking:** Adjacent to the arena, max 200 m.
- **Map:** Scale 1:5,000 / 1:3,500, contour interval 2.5 m. Created 2026.
- **Terrain:** University campus area with dense buildings combined with a trail-rich forest area featuring steep slopes in parts.
- **Quarantine for Championship Classes:** To ensure a fair competition, competitors in the championship classes (**HD21** and **HD17–20**) **must not** visit the arena at Syltahallen or its parking lot before their start. Competitors must travel directly to the start from the outside via the Model Event area. After finishing, competitors are free to visit the arena. _Tip: Leave your vehicle at OK Linné Clubhouse and cycle to the sprint start, or send your gear to the arena with companions._
- **Start:** First start at **16:30**. Orange/white tapes.
- **Open Classes:** Short, Medium, and Long. Direct registration at the arena between 16:00–17:30.
- **Maximum Time:** 2 hours.
- **Officials:** Course Setter Magnus Blåudd (OK Rodhen), Map Controllers Jonas Eklund & Jean-Charles Lallevee, Course Controller Berth-Arne Bengtsson.

---

## Long Distance – Sunday 16 August

- **Arena:** OK Linné Clubhouse, Tallbacksvägen 68 in SW Uppsala (GPS: `59.828125, 17.610964`). Signposted from Norbyvägen.
- **Parking:** Adjacent to the arena, max 300 m.
- **Map:** Scale 1:10,000 / 1:12,500, contour interval 2.5 m. Created 2019, revised 2026.
- **Terrain:** Nature reserve featuring an extensive, interconnected network of trails and gravel roads. Gentle to moderate relief with some steep hills.
- **Safety & Courtesy:** The area is a popular recreational area for walkers, cyclists, and grazing livestock. Keep to the right when passing oncoming trail users and announce yourself when overtaking. Potentially dangerous passages (drops/steep slopes) are marked with red/white tape. Sections affected by spruce bark beetle attacks are marked as out-of-bounds forbidden areas.
- **First Aid in Forest:** In addition to first aid at the arena, a first aid backpack is located in the terrain (marked with a red cross on the map). In emergency cases, call 112. The Race Director's phone number is printed on the maps.
- **Start:** First start at **10:00**. Start adjacent to the arena.
- **Open Classes:** Short, Medium, and Long. Direct registration at the arena between 09:30–11:00.
- **Maximum Time:** 4 hours.
- **Officials:** Race Director Lars Pontén (IF Thor), Course Setter Torbjörn Johansson (IF Thor).

